          "date": "2026-09-28T13:50:48Z"
        },
        "message": "Read a `**/` in a paths filter as zero or more directories (#389)\n\n* Read a `**/` in a paths filter as zero or more directories\n\n`patternToRegex` compiled `**` positionally, so `**/*.md` became\n`^.*\\/[^/]*\\.md$` and never matched a top-level file. GitHub fires the\nworkflow anyway, so willfire dropped that workflow's whole check set whenever\nthe only matching change was top-level — under-prediction, the direction that\nopens a silent hole in a pr-monitor gate.\n\nMeasured on #360: `**/*.txt` and `gdocs/**/*.md` both dispatched against\ntop-level files. The same probe confirms `?` and `+` already match GitHub\n(zero-or-one and one-or-more of the preceding character), so they are\nunchanged.\n\nFixes #359\n\nrelease: minor\n\n* e2e attestation for fix/glob-doublestar-slash\n\nrelease: minor",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "26129cb8c0af7c449b246a0627dd01a564983484",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/thekevinscott/willfire/git/trees/26129cb8c0af7c449b246a0627dd01a564983484"
